    "body": "### Contributing guidelines\n\n- [X] I have read [CONTRIBUTING.md](https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/blob/main/CONTRIBUTING.md)\n- [X] I have read [CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md](https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/blob/main/CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md)\n- [X] I have updated 'mini.nvim' to latest version\n\n### Module(s)\n\nmini.completeion\n\n### Description\n\nI have mini.completetion setup with mason-lsp.\r\nFor some reason I don't get any suggetsions of completion in my go file unless its something\r\nthat has been written in any of the open buffers.\r\n\n\n### Neovim version\n\n0.7.0\n\n### Steps to reproduce\n\n1. setup mini.completetion\r\n2. setup mason (lsp installer) from [this](https://github.com/williamboman/mason-lspconfig.nvim)\r\n3. downloaded the server (gopls)\n\n### Expected behavior\n\nAn autocompletetion in my go file \r\nFor example: If i write S i would like it to suggest Struct\r\nor if I type fmt. It should suggest functions from the fmt library\n\n### Actual behavior\n\nit doesn't suggest anything.\r\n\r\n![image](https://user-images.githubusercontent.com/91673569/193645747-3cc4e20b-d35f-411d-8b79-2d9d7567bfff.png)\r\n",
