            "author_association": "MEMBER",
            "body": "It doesn't look right now as a 'mini.completion' issue. Do you have other LSP servers set up? If yes, do they work (provide completion results from language server)?\r\n\r\nIt can be a misconfigured language server. One sure way to find out is this:\r\n- Add these lines somewhere inside your config:\r\n```lua\r\n_G.lsp_results = false\r\n_G.track_lsp = function()\r\n  _G.lsp_results = {}\r\n  vim.lsp.buf_request_all(\r\n    vim.api.nvim_get_current_buf(),\r\n    'textDocument/completion',\r\n    vim.lsp.util.make_position_params(),\r\n    function(result) table.insert(_G.lsp_results, result) end\r\n  )\r\nend\r\n\r\n-- Change `<M-m>` keybinding to your liking\r\nvim.keymap.set('i', '<M-m>', '<Cmd>lua _G.track_lsp()<CR>', {})\r\n```\r\n- When you expect to see an LSP completion result in Insert mode, type `<M-m>` (or other mapping, if you changed it).\r\n- Type `:lua print(vim.inspect(_G.lsp_results))` and look at output. It should contain a table with everything retrievable from LSP servers under that conditions. If it is empty, 'mini.completion' can do nothing. Look at how to configure LSP server.\r\n\r\nAnother thing might be a misconfigured 'mini.completion'. For example, what is the output of the following code: `:lua print(vim.inspect(vim.o[MiniCompletion.config.lsp_completion.source_func]))` ?",
