        {
            "author_association": "MEMBER",
            "body": "After looking at your config, I think this is a LSP misconfiguration issue.\r\n\r\nYou seem to have installed Go language server ([via 'williamboman/mason-lspconfig.nvim'](https://github.com/AutoAFK/VimConfig/blob/c6c356063244188a395ca4260c6c9c3478408613/init.lua#L37-L40)), but you didn't tell Neovim to automatically use it (attach) in Go files. You still need ['neovim/nvim-lspconfig'](https://github.com/neovim/nvim-lspconfig) for that (as it says in 'mason-lspconfig' docs).",
